<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.13.3: Writing Equations that Represent a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01971</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.13.3: Writing Equations that Represent a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d7d5b3f5-60d7-449c-8a85-f90f9088b74b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <media alt="insert alt text">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00001">Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Identify the
        function that matches each graph. Make sure your graph goes through all three points shown!</para>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Identify the function of Graph A.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 1, 1), (0, 0), and (1, 1). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_01.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00004">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00006"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Identify the function of Graph B.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 3, 0), (0, negative 9), and (3, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 10 to 2.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_02.svg"/>

            </media>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00009">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00011"><m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>9</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> or <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">Identify the function of Graph C.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 2, 0), (0.5, negative 6.25), and (3, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 10 to 2.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_03.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00014">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00015">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00016"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00017">Identify the function of Graph D.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 6, 0), (negative 3, negative 9), and (0, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 9 to 4. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 10 to 2.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_04.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00019">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00020">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00021"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00022">Identify the function of Graph E.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 2, 0), (0, 4), and (2, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_05.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00024">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00026"><m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> or <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00027">Identify the function of Graph F.</para>
          <para id="para-00028">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (0, 4), (2, 0), and (4, 4). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 4 to 8. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_06.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00029">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00030">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00031"><m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> or <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00032">Identify the function of Graph G.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 1, 0), (0, 3), and (3, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 4 to 8. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_07.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00034">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00037">Identify the function of Graph H.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (0, 5), (1, 0), and (5, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 4 to 8. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 5 to 7.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_08.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00039">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00040">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00041"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00042">Identify the function of Graph I.</para>
          <para id="para-00043">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 1, 2), (0, 0), and (1, 2). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 4 to 8.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_09.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00044">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00046"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00047">Identify the function of Graph J.</para>
          <para id="para-00048">
            <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 4, negative 4), (0, 0), and (4, negative 4). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 6 to 6. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 8 to 4.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_06_10.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00049">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00050">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00051"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0.25</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Video: Writing Equations that Represent a Quadratic Graph</title>
      <para id="para-00052">Watch the following video to learn more about writing equations that
        represent a quadratic graph.</para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/296f3aec8fb544a526585ba8f6a0ae3cdcf31337"/>
      </media>
    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
          <para id="para-00053"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_7_13_3_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00004">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Writing Quadratic Equations from Graphs</title>
        <para id="para-00055">Write an equation for the graph below:</para>
        <para id="para-00056">
          <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 2, 0), (1, negative 9), and (4, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 10 to 10. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 15 to 10.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_08_01.jpg" width="300"/>
          </media>

        </para>
        <para id="para-00057">First, locate the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-intercepts at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo>,</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo>,</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para><para id="para-00054">Next, write
          the factor for each <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-intercept.</para>
        <para id="para-00058">The factors that result in the given zeros are <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para><para id="para-00066">The equation
          for this quadratic function is <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00059">Use graphing technology to check your answer.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Writing Quadratic Equations from Graphs</title>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00011">
            <problem id="prob-00011">
              <para id="para-00060">Write an equation for the graph below:</para>
              <para id="para-00061">
                <media alt="A parabola on a coordinate grid. The parabola passes through 3 points that are labeled: (negative 6, 0), (negative 2, negative 16), and (2, 0). The x-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 15 to 15. The y-axis scale is 1 and extends from negative 20 to 7.5.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_15_08_02.jpg" width="300"/>
                </media>

              </para>
              <para id="para-00062">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
          button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00011">
              <para id="para-00063">Here is how to write an equation for the function graphed:</para>
              <para id="para-00064">First, identify the <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>-intercepts: <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>.</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> Next, write a
          factor for each zero: <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00065">The function in factored form is <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
